grok-alab runs xAI's Grok Build command-line program (`grok`) as a separate process. It
does not include, modify or redistribute any part of that program; `grok` is installed and
licensed separately, by xAI's terms, through aterm's package manager. Grok and Grok Build
are names of xAI.

Parts of grok-alab follow aterm's source (Apache-2.0, the same author): the package store
layout and build numbering of its package manager (crates/atpkg), and the per-vendor resume
grammar of its relaunch lanes (crates/aterm-agent/src/harness/relaunch.rs, lanes.rs). The
file and function each comes from is cited where it is used.
